   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "As Michael says, there&#39;s no reason to do this yourself.\r<br>The simplex data type for a parameter does this under the hood.\r<br>\r<br>But if you want to for some reason, then you will need\r<br>a lower=0,upper=1 constraint on q[N].  I didn&#39;t check your work\r<br>after that.  Just use prints to debug as you go to isolate where\r<br>things go wrong.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Aug 16, 2014, at 7:02 AM, Xiangze Dubian &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">xia...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>\r<br>&gt; Hi, \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I tried to run stick-breaking process in stan as well as 293 page of The BUGS book.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;  data{\r<br>&gt;  int&lt;lower=0&gt; C;//num of cludter\r<br>&gt;  int&lt;lower=0&gt; N;//data num\r<br>&gt;  real v[N];\r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  parameters {\r<br>&gt;  real amu;\r<br>&gt;  real bmu;\r<br>&gt;  vector[C] mu_mix;\r<br>&gt;  vector[C] tau_mix;\r<br>&gt;  real q[N];\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  transformed parameters{\r<br>&gt;  simplex [C] pi;\r<br>&gt;  real&lt;lower=0&gt; p[N];\r<br>&gt;  vector [C] mu_prec;\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  p[1] &lt;- q[1];\r<br>&gt;  for(j in 2:C)\r<br>&gt;  p[j] &lt;- q[j]*(1-q[j-1])*p[j-1]/q[j-1];\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  for(j in 1:C){\r<br>&gt;  pi[j] &lt;- p[j]/sum(p);\r<br>&gt;  mu_prec[j] &lt;- bmu*tau_mix[j];\r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  model {\r<br>&gt;  real bprec;\r<br>&gt;  real alpha;\r<br>&gt;  real aprec;\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  amu ~ normal(0,0.001);\r<br>&gt;  bmu ~ gamma(0.5,50);\r<br>&gt;  bprec~gamma(2,1);\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  alpha &lt;- 1;\r<br>&gt;  aprec&lt;-2;\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  for(j in 1:C){\r<br>&gt;  q[j]~beta(1,alpha);\r<br>&gt;  mu_mix[j]~normal(amu,mu_prec[j]);\r<br>&gt;  tau_mix[j]~gamma(aprec,bprec);\r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  for(i in 1:N){\r<br>&gt;  for(j in 1:C){\r<br>&gt;  increment_log_prob(\r<br>&gt;  pi[j]+normal_log(v[i],mu_mix[j],tau_mix[j])\r<br>&gt;  );\r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; #from BUGS book page 293\r<br>&gt; #Stick-breaking process\r<br>&gt; #<a href=\"http://www2.imm.dtu.dk/courses/02443/projects/Roeder_JASA_1990.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www2.imm.dtu.dk/courses/02443/projects/Roeder_JASA_1990.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466025019000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1WeGi5aT9iK2E-B6qvWIvi\">http://www2.imm.dtu.dk/courses/02443/projects/Roeder_JASA_1990.pdf</a>\r<br>&gt; library(rstan)\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; C &lt;- 10\r<br>&gt; data &lt;-read.csv(&quot;data.csv&quot;)\r<br>&gt; N &lt;-nrow(data)\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; model &lt;-stan_model(&quot;STB.stan&quot;)\r<br>&gt; fit &lt;- sampling(model,v=data,N=N,C=C, iter = 1000, chains = 1)\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; traceplot(fit, ask=T)\r<br>&gt; print(fit, digit=2)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/xiangze/4c3c54d73bc7668ad139\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/xiangze/4c3c54d73bc7668ad139&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466025019000&amp;usg=AOvVaw14pcCwQShzn5eyOuguyB_P\">https://gist.github.com/xiangze/4c3c54d73bc7668ad139</a>\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; The compile process of this code seems successfully done. But the sampling process stopped with the following messages.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Invalid value of pi: Error in function validate transformed params N4stan5agrad3varE: pi\r<br>&gt; pi is not a valid simplex. The element at 5 is -0.719628:0, but should be greater than or equal to 0\r<br>&gt; Rejecting proposed initial value with zero density.\r<br>&gt; Initialization failed after 100 attempts. Try specifying initial values, reducing ranges of constrained values, or reparameterizing the model.\r<br>&gt; error occurred during calling the sampler; sampling not done\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Is this error caused by insufficient coding or internal restriction of stan?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Regards,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Xiangze\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
